#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171799 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d12e0d62-7d0c-55d3-aaf4-d37fe5d691bf" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Normal Vector to a Parametric Surface Given Some Parameter Values"}] :question/id #uuid "78a80655-36ca-5628-b11a-4ac492b7cb3e" :question/math-academy-id "e-8938" :question/problem "Compute a normal vector to the parametric surface defined by the equations\n$x=u, \\quad y=1+u^2, \\quad z=v^2$\nat the point where $u=1$ and $v=2$." :question/worked-solution "In vector form, our surface has the equation\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\big\\langle u, \\: 1 + u^2, \\: v^2\\big\\rangle\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr_{u}^{′}(u, v) &= ⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u}, \\frac{∂y}{∂u}, \\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u), \\frac{∂}{∂u}(1 + u^{2}), \\frac{∂}{∂u}(v^{2})⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨1, 2u, 0⟩ \\\\\nr_{v}^{′}(u, v) &= ⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v}, \\frac{∂y}{∂v}, \\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u), \\frac{∂}{∂v}(1 + u^{2}), \\frac{∂}{∂v}(v^{2})⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨0, 0, 2v⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=1$ and $v=2{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr_{u}^{′}(1, 2) &= ⟨1, 2(1), 0⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨1, 2, 0⟩ \\\\\nr_{v}^{′}(1, 2) &= ⟨0, 0, 2(2)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨0, 0, 4⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface at the point where $u=1$ and $v=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nn &= r_{u}^{′}(1, 2) \\cdot r_{v}^{′}(1, 2) \\\\\n&=\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= ⟨\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{vmatrix}, -\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{vmatrix},\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨8,-4, 0⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171800 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "42bb08b6-6e41-51e9-853f-cd28a5c35a2c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Normal Vector to a Parametric Surface Given a Point on the Surface"}] :question/id #uuid "da389dec-eca9-5f6c-8487-fdcbc0cca227" :question/math-academy-id "e-8939" :question/problem "Compute a normal vector to the parametric surface generated by the vector-valued function $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)= \\big\\langle u^2-2, \\: u-v, \\: v^3+1 \\big\\rangle$ at the point $(-1,2,0)$." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $(-1,2,0)$ lies on the surface, we obtain\n\n$$\n{u^{2} - 2 =-1; u - v = 2; v^{3} + 1 = 0\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr_{u}^{′}(u, v) &= ⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u}, \\frac{∂y}{∂u}, \\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u^{2} - 2), \\frac{∂}{∂u}(u - v), \\frac{∂}{∂u}(v^{3} + 1)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨2u, 1, 0⟩ \\\\\nr_{v}^{′}(u, v) &= ⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v}, \\frac{∂y}{∂v}, \\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u^{2} - 2), \\frac{∂}{∂v}(u - v), \\frac{∂}{∂v}(v^{3} + 1)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨0,-1, 3v^{2}⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=1$ and $v=-1{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr_{u}^{′}(1,-1) &= ⟨2(1), 1, 0⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨2, 1, 0⟩ \\\\\nr_{v}^{′}(1,-1) &= ⟨0,-1, 3(-1)^{2}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨0,-1, 3⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface at the point $(3,1,0)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nn &= r_{u}^{′}(1,-1) \\cdot r_{v}^{′}(1,-1) \\\\\n&=\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= ⟨\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{vmatrix}, -\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix},\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨3,-6,-2⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171801 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7bed4e59-ea2f-5060-9beb-e52473607292" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of the Tangent Plane to a Parametric Surface Given Some Parameter Values"}] :question/id #uuid "a5f4a28a-c56d-5c26-bb55-fd6b8b4424cd" :question/math-academy-id "e-8940" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface generated by the vector-valued function $\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\big\\langle v^2, \\: u-v, \\: u^2 \\big\\rangle$ at the point where $u=2$ and $v=-1$." :question/worked-solution "We first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr_{u}^{′}(u, v) &= ⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u}, \\frac{∂y}{∂u}, \\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v^{2}), \\frac{∂}{∂u}(u - v), \\frac{∂}{∂u}(u^{2})⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨0, 1, 2u⟩ \\\\\nr_{v}^{′}(u, v) &= ⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v}, \\frac{∂y}{∂v}, \\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v^{2}), \\frac{∂}{∂v}(u - v), \\frac{∂}{∂v}(u^{2})⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨2v,-1, 0⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these vectors when $u=2$ and $v=-1{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr_{u}^{′}(2,-1) &= ⟨0, 1, 2(2)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨0, 1, 4⟩ \\\\\nr_{v}^{′}(2,-1) &= ⟨2(-1),-1, 0⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨ - 2,-1, 0⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nn &= r_{u}^{′}(2,-1) \\cdot r_{v}^{′}(2,-1) \\\\\n&=\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= ⟨\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}, -\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{vmatrix},\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨4,-8, 2⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the parameters $u=2$ and $v=-1$ correspond to the point\n\n$$\n\\big((-1)^2, \\: 2-(-1), \\: 2^2 \\big) = (1, 3, 4)\n$$\n\nthe equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nn \\cdot ⟨x - x_{0}, y - y_{0}, z - z_{0}⟩ &= 0 \\\\\n⟨4,-8, 2⟩ \\cdot ⟨x - 1, y - 3, z - 4⟩ &= 0 \\\\\n4 \\cdot (x - 1) + (-8) \\cdot (y - 3) + 2 \\cdot (z - 4) &= 0 \\\\\n4x - 8y + 2z + 12 &= 0 \\\\\n2x - 4y + z + 6 &= 0 \\\\\n2x - 4y + z &= -6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171802 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d5da71e-534c-57b6-9b55-0d85d01f1b9c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of the Tangent Plane to a Parametric Surface Given a Point on the Surface"}] :question/id #uuid "b4914ab3-353a-5c74-9126-0358177e2025" :question/math-academy-id "e-8941" :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface defined by the equations\n$x=u+v, \\quad y=3u^2, \\quad z=u-v$\nat the point $(2,3, 0)$." :question/worked-solution "In vector form, our surface has the equation\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\big\\langle u+v, \\: 3u^2, \\: u-v \\big\\rangle\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that since $(2, 3, 0)$ lies on the surface, we obtain\n\n$$\n{u + v = 2; 3u^{2} = 3; u - v = 0\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr_{u}^{′}(u, v) &= ⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u}, \\frac{∂y}{∂u}, \\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u + v), \\frac{∂}{∂u}(3u^{2}), \\frac{∂}{∂u}(u - v)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨1, 6u, 1⟩ \\\\\nr_{v}^{′}(u, v) &= ⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v}, \\frac{∂y}{∂v}, \\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u + v), \\frac{∂}{∂v}(3u^{2}), \\frac{∂}{∂v}(u - v)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨1, 0,-1⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate these tangent vectors when $u=1$ and $v=1{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr_{u}^{′}(1, 1) &= ⟨1, 6(1), 1⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨1, 6, 1⟩ \\\\\nr_{v}^{′}(1, 1) &= ⟨1, 0,-1⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the surface is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nn &= r_{u}^{′}(1, 1) \\cdot r_{v}^{′}(1, 1) \\\\\n&=\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 6 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= ⟨\\begin{vmatrix}6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{vmatrix}, -\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix},\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨ - 6, 2,-6⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the tangent plane is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nn \\cdot ⟨x - x_{0}, y - y_{0}, z - z_{0}⟩ &= 0 \\\\\n⟨ - 6, 2,-6⟩ \\cdot ⟨x - 2, y - 3, z⟩ &= 0 \\\\\n(-6) \\cdot (x - 2) + 2 \\cdot (y - 3) + (-6) \\cdot z &= 0 \\\\\n- 6x + 2y - 6z + 6 &= 0 \\\\\n- 3x + y - 3z + 3 &= 0 \\\\\n3x - y + 3z &= 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172154 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d12e0d62-7d0c-55d3-aaf4-d37fe5d691bf" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Normal Vector to a Parametric Surface Given Some Parameter Values"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf9b9227-6a90-5d08-8c54-d3c25854f3ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1, 1, 1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168128} {:answer/id #uuid "e066f492-305d-5ace-a616-33596f73cfa1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,-4, 0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168129} {:answer/id #uuid "ed6268a5-c9c0-5590-bec2-3616e0b61baf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,-1,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168130} {:answer/id #uuid "19e81edf-df1a-5832-b39a-b8c59821ad8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4, 1,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168131} {:answer/id #uuid "5b051447-66d5-539d-acd9-a9765d71b420" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1, 4, 0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168132}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed6268a5-c9c0-5590-bec2-3616e0b61baf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,-1,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168130} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e2b0a22-f9ad-55e2-bcf0-35f112581707" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168127}] :question/id #uuid "9eacf6e9-24ec-5d35-b5ca-6a839ae4584e" :question/math-academy-id "q-105544" :question/problem "Compute a normal vector to the parametric surface defined by the equations\n\n$x = u + v, y = u^{2}v, z = v$\nat the point where $u = 1$ and $v = 2$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172156 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7bed4e59-ea2f-5060-9beb-e52473607292" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of the Tangent Plane to a Parametric Surface Given Some Parameter Values"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c69073d7-a2ba-5855-8f2f-77bff8b593dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x - z = 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186168140} {:answer/id #uuid "f1a916a4-6e28-5870-8c8d-9b92d83